Hmmm, well, having refereed soccer for years, I think pretty much
anything with an accessible underside can probably be kicked
aloft, but just in case:

YANI: Boots of WedgeToe-ed-ness

Player character kicking while wearing these boots can loft _any_
object, and monsters of size small, into the air and across the
usual kicking distance. Monsters of size small will take both
to-hit damage, _and_ falling damage. Objects kicked aloft may
(40% chance) completely miss monsters of size small in the
intervening grid cells. Monsters hit by an aloft kicked weapon
take damage as for backstabbing, for non-weapon, non-potion as if
the object had been thrown. Potions kicked by these boots have a
10% chance of blowing up in the adventurer's face rather than
striking the intended target. Small monsters kicked aloft to land
on stairs or in a pit have an 80% chance of falling down stairs
or entering the pit, and take both sorts of damage, falling from
aloft, and falling into a pit or down stairs, plus the initial
to-hit damage.

